git -C $csrbt commit -m "ADR-201: every record carries its photographs -- one shared component, the Darwin Core column that was missing, and the address the refusal named" `
  -m "ONE PAGE IN THIS KIT TOOK A PHOTOGRAPH AND TWENTY DID NOT, on a kit that emits Darwin Core -- and associatedMedia, the term whose whole job is to name the frames, WAS NOT IN THE COLUMN LIST AT ALL, so every deposit this kit has ever produced left its media unnamed. THE RECORD CARRIES THE REFERENCE, NOT THE IMAGE: a CSV cell cannot hold a JPEG, a base64 photograph inside a .eco export turns a 40 kB record into a 4 MB one, and Darwin Core asks the term for an IDENTIFIER OF the media rather than the media. So what travels is filename, bytes, captured, crc32. CRC-32 AND NOT SHA-256, DELIBERATELY: crypto.subtle does not exist on a file:// page because a file URL is not a secure context, and this kit is opened off a card in the field as often as it is served over https as an artifact; a digest available in one of those two is worse than a weaker one that gives the SAME ANSWER IN BOTH, because the point is that the number written on the sheet in the field still matches the number computed back at the desk. It is an INTEGRITY check and must not be called cryptographic, and the suite asserts the STANDARD check value, crc32('123456789') = cbf43926. ``captured`` is File.lastModified -- the file's mtime, not EXIF -- and the pages say so. Images never leave the tab. ONE COMPONENT, NOT TEN COPIES OF A FILE READER: FEK.photos lives in the shared entry layer every data-entry page inlines, because a file reader copied into ten sheets is ten places for a checksum to be computed differently. It carries its own live region by ADR-199's rule, so a file that is not an image is REFUSED OUT LOUD, NAMING IT; and set() deliberately cannot put a photograph back, because a page cannot hand a File to a file input and restoring one from a record would be restoring a caption. Nine pages mount it. The stand sheet is NOT migrated -- its pane carries a Link species button the component knows nothing about, and that is two changes wearing one hat -- but it takes the shared checksum so one column has one meaning. THE ADDRESS THE REFUSAL NAMED: drop-files has always taken a control of kind drop_zone and the refusal a bad address earns has always ADVERTISED @kind=drop_zone, while KINDS -- the list every snapshot is built from -- did not carry it; it lived in swarm.py, which only the swarm reads. ADR-141'S RULE BACKWARDS. The check is written over the POOLS rather than over the one kind that prompted it, and it immediately found a second: set-checkbox pools ``checkbox``, in the same private list. Two more rules came out of the fix -- the zone is found by THE MARK THE CAPTURE LEAVES, the same data-h-drop attribute drop-files checks before it dispatches; and NO KIND IS LISTED TWICE, because a kind listed twice is discovered twice, the selectors renumber, and a diff reports controls appearing that nobody added. FOUR THINGS THIS SLICE FOUND THAT WERE NOT ITS SUBJECT. Three checks in verify_report failed on the COMMITTED ADR-200 TREE when run outside run_all: the page autosaves on a debounce and the widget it renders arrived after the baseline snapshot, so the check passed or failed on machine load; the suite now waits for two observations to agree on the stamp. A ``typeof x === `"function`"`` guard turned a WRONG FUNCTION NAME into silence on the survey design, whose export writer is outOut(). Three exports said 'nothing logged' whatever else the session held -- A SESSION THAT IS ONLY PHOTOGRAPHS IS STILL A SESSION. And FOUR OF THE NINE CARDS WERE INSERTED BETWEEN PANES rather than inside one, so they rendered on every tab at once; the kit's pane invariants are all about which pane is SHOWING and none asked whether a card is in one at all, so there is a check for that now, read off the rendered document rather than the source. verify_fek 101 -> 122, verify_harness 28 -> 33, verify_dwc 150 -> 154, verify_report 242 -> 248, verify_walk unchanged at 126 with the drop zone off its unreachable list. mutate_fek is NEW -- the one file nineteen pages inline had no mutant runner at all -- 13 mutants all killed; mutate_harness 18 -> 22 and its runner now runs BOTH harness suites; mutate_report 145 -> 149. Twenty artifacts republished and measured at the URL." `
  -m "Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>" -m "Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YPcb1A7CejriRgL9xLrhJ3"
